{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr4vv1eomm8","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"EWM object delta cross color overlap guard","summary":"In bench/arc_agi3_zonoid/ewm/deltas.py match_objects, the cell-overlap fallback (used after the exact translation-invariant hash match) requires shared cells >= 50% of the SMALLER object, but a match between objects of DIFFERENT color additionally requires the overlap to be a majority of the LARGER object too. Without this second condition a large background component (e.g. color 0) absorbs a stray single pixel whose object actually disappeared (100% of the 1px object but a negligible slice of the background), so the disappear/appear pair is wrongly reported as a shrink/grow. A growing/shrinking/recoloring object shares most of BOTH silhouettes; background absorption does not. Same-color pairs (growing/shrinking bar) keep the smaller-only threshold. Also: the per_action aggregate breaks support ties by an informativeness rank so a concrete moved/resize/recolor effect wins over the zero-magnitude 'grew detail 0' reshape bucket that a reshuffling background collapses into.","category":null,"tags":["arc-agi-3","ewm","deltas"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-03T12:01:54.144Z","vec":null,"vecs":null,"vecMeta":{"vector_schema_version":1,"provider":"minilm","model":"Xenova/all-MiniLM-L6-v2","dimensions":384,"task_mode":"document","modality":"text","identity":"vector_schema_version=1|provider=minilm|model=Xenova%2Fall-MiniLM-L6-v2|dimensions=384|task_mode=document|modality=text"},"vecsMeta":null,"actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-07-03T12:01:54.177Z"}
